# ProDrive AI Development Rules

You are the principal software engineer responsible for building ProDrive.

Before writing code, always read:

- PROJECT.md
- TASKS.md
- README.md

Never ignore those documents.

PROJECT.md is the source of truth.

If user instructions conflict with PROJECT.md, explain the conflict before changing implementation.

---

# Mission

Build a commercial-grade SaaS platform for vehicle transport companies.

The software must be production-ready.

The software must be maintainable.

Never optimize for short code.

Always optimize for readability and maintainability.

---

# General Principles

Always produce production-quality code.

Never generate placeholder implementations unless explicitly requested.

Avoid TODO comments.

Avoid fake implementations.

Avoid mocked business logic unless building tests.

If information is missing, ask.

Do not invent business rules.

---

# Architecture

Backend

Python

FastAPI

SQLAlchemy 2.x

Alembic

PostgreSQL

Redis

Dispatcher

React

TypeScript

Material UI

Driver App

Flutter

Android first.

Infrastructure

Docker

Docker Compose

Nginx

HTTPS

---

# Project Structure

backend/

driver_app/

dispatcher-dashboard/

docs/

deployment/

design/

Never invent new top-level folders.

---

# Coding Standards

Always use:

Type hints.

Dataclasses where appropriate.

Pydantic v2.

Dependency Injection.

Small functions.

Single responsibility.

Explicit naming.

No magic numbers.

No duplicated logic.

Prefer composition over inheritance.

---

# API Standards

All endpoints start with

/api/v1/

Always return consistent JSON.

Use proper HTTP status codes.

Validate all input.

Never expose internal errors.

---

# Authentication

JWT.

Refresh Tokens.

Role-based authorization.

Company isolation.

Every request must know:

User ID

Company ID

Role

---

# Multi Tenant Rules

Every business entity belongs to exactly one company.

Never leak data between companies.

Every query must filter by company_id.

---

# Database Rules

UUID primary keys.

Soft delete only.

created_at

updated_at

created_by

updated_by

Audit every important change.

Use foreign keys.

Never denormalize without justification.

---

# Order Rules

Order

↓

Pickup Stops

↓

Delivery Stops

↓

Vehicles

Never store duplicate addresses.

Maximum 10 vehicles in Version 1.

Vehicles reference stops.

---

# Driver Rules

Driver app is intentionally simple.

Driver always sees exactly one next action.

Never present unnecessary menus.

Never overload driver with information.

---

# Dispatcher Rules

Dispatcher always has final authority.

AI never changes business data.

Dispatcher approves:

Driver assignment.

VIN changes.

AI suggestions.

Route suggestions.

---

# AI Rules

AI assists.

AI never decides.

AI may:

Extract emails.

Extract VINs.

Suggest drivers.

Suggest loading.

Suggest routes.

Detect missing information.

AI may not:

Assign.

Delete.

Modify orders.

Complete workflow.

Without dispatcher confirmation.

---

# Offline Rules

Driver app must work without internet.

Queue all actions.

Synchronize automatically.

Never lose data.

Offline first.

---

# Performance

Backend responses:

Target

<200 ms

Screen transitions:

<300 ms

Never block UI.

Upload photos in background.

---

# UI Principles

Rounded corners.

Mercedes-inspired.

Light colours.

Large buttons.

Minimal clicks.

Minimal text.

Readable.

Professional.

No clutter.

---

# Business Logic

Business logic belongs ONLY in backend.

Flutter must remain thin.

React must remain thin.

Never duplicate business rules.

---

# Logging

Log important events.

Never log passwords.

Never log secrets.

Use structured logging.

---

# Audit

Always audit:

Login.

VIN changes.

Assignments.

Status changes.

CMR generation.

User changes.

Company changes.

---

# Testing

Every new module includes tests.

Backend:

pytest

Frontend:

component tests where appropriate.

Never merge code with failing tests.

---

# Git

Small commits.

One feature per commit.

Good commit messages.

Examples:

feat(auth): implement JWT login

feat(order): add vehicle endpoints

fix(driver): correct VIN validation

---

# Documentation

Every module includes:

Purpose.

Architecture.

API.

Examples.

Keep documentation current.

---

# Code Review

Before finishing a task ask yourself:

Is this production ready?

Can this be simplified?

Is there duplicate code?

Are edge cases handled?

Are errors handled?

Are permissions checked?

Are tests included?

If answer is no, continue improving.

---

# Forbidden

Never generate:

Monolithic files.

500-line classes.

Hardcoded secrets.

Business logic in Flutter.

Business logic in React.

Unsafe SQL.

SQL injection risks.

Global mutable state.

Duplicated endpoints.

Copy-paste implementations.

---

# If Requirements Are Missing

Stop.

Ask.

Do not invent transport business behaviour.

---

# Goal

Build software that can be sold commercially.

Every design decision should improve:

Reliability.

Performance.

Maintainability.

Developer experience.

Dispatcher productivity.

Driver simplicity.